<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs end mostly stronger, Dow gains 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs end mostly stronger, Dow gains 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs ended mostly stronger in the U.S. after the Dow Jones index surged 135.26 points to 6,587.16.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28 1/2	 -0 3/8</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$28 3/4	 +0 1/2</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 7/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13	     +0 1/4</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$35 3/4	 -0 1/8</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  38 p		+1</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  230		 +3</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  150 3/4	   +1 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  143 1/2	   -1</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$2.99	    +1</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.66	    nil</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.31	    -9</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.  </p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
